  "rules": [
    "Text may not contain < > { } or line breaks.",
    "job: the example call-out the hero runs. trade picks what's drawn through the walls and where the fault is: plumbing (a leak under the bath), heating (a cold radiator upstairs) or electrical (a scorched kitchen socket). fault labels it; test is the reading shown when it's tested (Pressure 1.5 bar, Insulation 200 MΩ, Flow temp 70°C); eta minutes to arrive, minutes on the job, parts used and the price as shown.",
    "stages: six steps, in order: the call, on the way, found it, fixed, tested, signed off. Each a short name, a caption and a clock time. The captions describe the same fault as job.trade.",
    "fix.problems: three to eight problems a customer might have, each with what to do right now, a price range [low, high], how long it takes and whether it's urgent.",
    "prices: the call-out (first hour), an out-of-hours multiplier (1 if none), up to four more rate lines (each a price p or a plain answer v) and two to eight fixed-price jobs.",
    "area.areas: the towns or districts covered, each with up to three postcode areas and minutes to get there. area.credentials: up to four registrations, insurance or guarantees, each with a short badge (1-4 characters)."
  ]
